From: be7000-openwrt <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: ipq9574: give the MDIO controller the TCSR ethernet LDO register

The stock firmware sets the TCSR "ethernet LDO ready" bit (0x19475c4
bit 0) before it resets the PHY package. mdio-ipq4019 does the same,
but only when the device tree hands it that register as the second
reg entry (as the IPQ50xx trees do). The IPQ9574 tree never did, so
OpenWrt never set the bit.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574.dtsi
index 1cc3479..d57ce8e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574.dtsi
@@ -296,7 +296,8 @@
 
 		mdio: mdio@90000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,ipq9574-mdio", "qcom,ipq4019-mdio";
-			reg = <0x00090000 0x64>;
+			reg = <0x00090000 0x64>,
+			      <0x019475c4 0x4>;
 			pinctrl-0 = <&mdio_pins>;
 			pinctrl-names = "default";
 			#address-cells = <1>;
